            <ArticleTitle>Mechanical therapy for low back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>511-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pop.2012.06.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Physical therapy and manual medicine for low back pain encompass many different treatment modalities. There is a vast variety of techniques that physical therapists commonly use in the treatment of low back pain. Some of the therapies include, but are certainly not limited to, education, exercise, lumbar traction, manual manipulation, application of heat, cryotherapy, and ultrasonography. Many of these approaches are discussed specifically in this article.</AbstractText>
